meta {
  name: Sign in (email and password)
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Origin: {{webOrigin}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "lucamandelli@example.com",
    "password": "luca-de-obra-123"
  }
}

docs {
  Authenticates with email and password and returns a new session, writing the
  cookie over the previous one. Use it after sign-up to simulate someone coming
  back to the app on another device.

  **Responses you will see**

  | Status | When |
  | --- | --- |
  | 200 | Authenticated, session cookie renewed |
  | 401 | Wrong password, or an email that does not exist |
  | 403 | `Origin` missing or `null` (see the collection docs) |
  | 429 | More than 5 attempts in the same minute, per IP |

  The 429 is the rate limit doing its job against brute force, not a defect in
  the collection. It clears on its own after a minute.
}
